# Command mdfried

## What does this command do:

A markdown viewer for the terminal that renders images and Big Headers.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: curl -sSfL https://github.com/benjajaja/mdfried/releases/latest/download/mdfried -o ~/.local/bin/mdfried && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/mdfried
For Raspberry Pi install using: sudo apt install -y libchafa-dev && cargo install --locked mdfried
For Mac install using: curl -sSfL https://github.com/benjajaja/mdfried/releases/latest/download/mdfried_macos_aarch64 -o ~/.local/bin/mdfried && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/mdfried && xattr -d com.apple.quarantine ~/.local/bin/mdfried

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/mdfried
For Raspberry Pi run: ~/.cargo/bin/mdfried
For Mac run: ~/.local/bin/mdfried

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/benjajaja/mdfried

## Command options

Usage: mdfried [OPTIONS] [SOURCE]

  [SOURCE]  Markdown source: a file path, a URL, a "github:owner/repo" ref,
            or '-' / omit for stdin.

  -d, --deep-fry                            Extra deep fried images.
  -w, --watch                               Watch the markdown file, reload on changes.
  -s, --setup                               Force font setup (again).
      --print-config                        Write a mostly complete config example to stdout.
      --no-cap-checks                       Do not query the terminal stdin for capabilities.
      --debug-override-protocol-type <P>    Force graphics protocol to a specific type.
      --log [<FILE>]                        Log with RUST_LOG to FILE, or stderr if omitted.
  -h, --help                                Print help.
  -V, --version                             Print version.

# View a local markdown file
mdfried ./README.md

# Read from stdin (pipe markdown in)
cat notes.md | mdfried -
mdfried < notes.md

# Render a README straight from a GitHub repo
mdfried github:benjajaja/mdfried

# Render a markdown file at a URL
mdfried https://raw.githubusercontent.com/benjajaja/mdfried/master/README.md

# Live-reload while editing
mdfried --watch ./draft.md

# Re-run interactive font setup
mdfried --setup

# Print an example config to a new config file
mdfried --print-config > ~/.config/mdfried/config.toml

